{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446828-aeon-la-blessure","id":1446828,"title":"[Aeon] La Blessure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-01T12:43:28-07:00","id":1446828,"title":"[Aeon] La Blessure","content":"It's not clear to me: why the people that live in La Blessure don't simply leave? Is there a canon reason?<br /> <br /> (PS: I get that this enables Mad-Max-esque adventures, and that's cool, but I can't see why people in-scenario wouldn't simply flee &quot;the wasteland&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T12:49:21-07:00","id":1446833,"title":"","content":"Most of them are dead, the ones that remain were exposed to a high dose of Quantum Flux, so they are deformed and stained by it. If they try to flee, the army will hunt them as Aberrants. There are teams going around and helping people there, so it\u2019s not really mad Max and more like a area destroyed by war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T13:21:34-07:00","id":1446836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446828-aeon-la-blessure#post1446828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not clear to me: why the people that live in La Blessure don't simply leave? Is there a canon reason?<br /> <br /> (PS: I get that this enables Mad-Max-esque adventures, and that's cool, but I can't see why people in-scenario wouldn't simply flee &quot;the wasteland&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Flee to where? The surrounding countries are already flooded with refugees and don't want any more undocumented immigrants entering their territory. Beyond that, anyone testing positive for corruption will not be allowed past border checkpoints, and a lot of the people left in the area are now afflicted with corruption effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T13:55:15-07:00","id":1446844,"title":"","content":"If it was up to me, I would make a big change in the Blessure.<br /> <br /> First I would make the corporative paradise in Europe, with corporations taking control of EU and turning into something closer to FSA.<br /> <br /> USA would be the post Apocalyptic blessure, with most of the big cities damaged during aberrant war or nuclear attacks the government made in desperation to get rid of some more powerful Aberrants or because some Aberrants took control of nuclear missiles (or the combination of the 3). The results would be a USA with less than 25% of the population with lots of QFZ and big enough to be hard to scape walking.<br /> <br /> Maybe the wall was still up, so Mexicans are using it for their own safety, and Canadians are not luckier than Americans, as most of the population lives so close to USA they lost some of their big cities or were invaded by the running survivals of the American cities, and the country side would not have the same quantum flux, but yet the weather is not the best to live long lives in the wild.<br /> <br /> It would change a bit the setting, Orgotech would be in UK, that is not part of Facist EU, but not a great place to live as EU keeps UK in a bad economic situation, and Orgotech would be the reason UK is recovering after Brexit, Aberrant War and EU pressure.<br /> <br /> The Aesculapian Order base would still be somewhere in Europe, but probably out of EU, Zurich seams a good option, after EU tried to dismantle the order and split the assets among the local pharma industry, the order moved out of EU and got some Investments from the banks charity (yea, the banks are good... probably to pay less taxes...).<br /> <br /> Aeon Trinity moved their HQ from Chicago to Olympus before Aberrant War to incentive Lunar colonization. It saved them from the destruction of Chicago, but took them as hostage during Olympus hostage. The Head of the organization was not there, as there were a lot of risk in moving to Luna by the time, so they were working in several offices they had around the world.<br /> <br /> Basically that my changes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T14:03:28-07:00","id":1446845,"title":"","content":"^ The above!! <br /> <br /> Making Europe the corporate state and the US the post-apocalytpic location works for me. Much more then the current FSA to be honest. <br /> <br /> My changes would have the US still existing in enclaves trying to rebuild. Aeon still lies in America and thanks to its Inspired support survived intact. <br /> <br /> But yeah I like the above entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T22:41:24-07:00","id":1447350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446828-aeon-la-blessure?p=1446836#post1446836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flee to where? The surrounding countries are already flooded with refugees and don't want any more undocumented immigrants entering their territory. Beyond that, anyone testing positive for corruption will not be allowed past border checkpoints, and a lot of the people left in the area are now afflicted with corruption effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. The vast majority of the original population in what is now La Blessure died during or shortly after the impact, or were among the survivors who fled to other nations. What you have left are people too stubborn to leave, people who test positive for Corruption or have criminal records, and can't leave, and people who simply waited too long to leave, and are now in refugee camps on the border, because by the time they tried to leave, every nation who was willing to take in refugees weren't interested in taking in more. In addition, there are relief workers, Aberrant hunters, and looters, who have all gone into this area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:01:33-07:00","id":1447473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446828-aeon-la-blessure?p=1447350#post1447350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 1) (...) and are now in refugee camps on the border<br /> 2) (...) because by the time they tried to leave, every nation who was willing to take in refugees weren't interested in taking in more.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) if by &quot;border&quot; you mean &quot;in the inside part of La Blessure's border&quot;, that doesn't make a lot of sense... why wouldn't I live in the outer fringes, if there isn't an army ore something like that frbidding?<br /> <br /> 2) I find this (and the prospect of an Army or the like blocking the escape) something that goes completely against the Tone of AEON era, especially in Europe. That's something only FSA would do in practice.<br /> <br /> I really prefer the &quot;headcanon&quot; created by my brother: he defined that people in La Blessure were affected by the Taint/Corruption, and those who survived are now adapted to live there (even if they doesn't have any Transformations). But it goes beyond that: they now NEED the Corrupted/Tainted ambient of La Blessure to survive; if they leave to a non-Quantum-Flux zone, they'll die. They are essentially biologically dependent of the Corrupted area to live. (We haven't thought about all the consequences yet, but for now, this seems a much better in-game reason).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:15:17-07:00","id":1447479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446828-aeon-la-blessure?p=1447473#post1447473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really prefer the &quot;headcanon&quot; created by my brother: he defined that people in La Blessure were affected by the Taint/Corruption, and those who survived are now adapted to live there (even if they doesn't have any Transformations). But it goes beyond that: they now NEED the Corrupted/Tainted ambient of La Blessure to survive; if they leave to a non-Quantum-Flux zone, they'll die. They are essentially biologically dependent of the Corrupted area to live. (We haven't thought about all the consequences yet, but for now, this seems a much better in-game reason).</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not a bad explanation. If you want to give more action to that you can make them not only biologically dependent to it, but also more sensible to quantum control, putting them almost in direct control of any mind controller Aberrant present, a bit like a Zerg infected Terrans, that may or may not be killing machines or bestial creatures, but will attack unquestionably if commanded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T18:29:15-07:00","id":1447507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446828-aeon-la-blessure?p=1447473#post1447473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) I find this (and the prospect of an Army or the like blocking the escape) something that goes completely against the Tone of AEON era, especially in Europe. That's something only FSA would do in practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>How did you come to that conclusion? Compare a map of modern Europe to the European setting info in the Aeon core book.<br /> <br /> France, Belgium, and the Netherlands are la Blessure.<br /> <br /> To the northeast are Germany and Austria. They've fractured into minor city-states, with the eastern portion getting eaten by militarily aggressive neighbors and the western portion overrun by la Blessure refugees.<br /> <br /> To the east is Switzerland, home to a growing extremist isolationist movement.<br /> <br /> To the southeast is Italy, which is described as having &quot;a surprisingly brutal police force.&quot; They accept thousands (only thousands?) of la Blessure refugees every year, then ship them off to other countries.<br /> <br /> Spain is to the south. It is fractured and being economically overpowered by Portugal. The northern region is on the verge of economic collapse due to the influx of la Blessure refugees.<br /> <br /> To the north is England (The United Republic). It is a repressive isolationist nation that, &quot;guards its coastal borders ferociously against refugees. The media fans the flames of xenophobia against foreigners.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}